    "# Lab 5a: Capture, Open-Weight 3D Generation & Local `gsplat` Reconstruction\n",
    "**Course:** CIS 536 / 736 - Computer Graphics (Fall 2026)  \n",
    "**Phase 3:** Generative Assets & Neural Rendering | **Module 8:** Generative Geometry & 3D Gaussian Splatting (Lectures 25–27)  \n",
    "**Associated Assignment:** MP 7 — Generative Geometry & `gsplat` Reconstruction\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective & Hardware Constraints\n",
    "In this laboratory session, you will execute both halves of the **Module 8 / MP 7** local neural rendering and generative geometry workflow within an **8GB VRAM floor**:\n",
    "1. **Part 1 (Environment & VRAM Floor Verification):** Verify local CUDA/PyTorch availability, inspect available GPU memory, and confirm that `colmap`, `ffmpeg`, `gsplat`, and OpenUSD (`pxr`) are accessible.\n",
    "2. **Part 2 (Open-Weight 3D Generation & OpenUSD Export — MP 7 Part 1):** Generate 2 candidate 3D assets locally using open-weight diffusion models (`Point-E` / `Shap-E`) across distinct prompts or seeds, critique their geometric fidelity, and export the selected mesh to an **OpenUSD (`.usda`)** stage ready for Unity 6.\n",
    "3. **Part 3 (Multi-View Capture & COLMAP Structure-from-Motion — Lecture 26 & 27):** Extract 30–50 sharp frames (capped at $1920 \\times 1080$ to respect the 8GB VRAM floor) from a multi-view capture sequence and run COLMAP (`feature_extractor`, `matcher`, `mapper`, `image_undistorter`) to recover camera intrinsics, extrinsics, and the initial sparse point cloud.\n",
    "4. **Part 4 (3D Gaussian Splatting Mathematics & Local `gsplat` Training — MP 7 Part 2):** Verify the positive semi-definite covariance factorization ($\\Sigma = R S S^\\top R^\\top$), Spherical Harmonics (SH) view-dependent color evaluation, and adaptive density control (cloning, splitting, pruning), then train your scene in `gsplat` and export the `.ply` radiance field."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 1: Environment Bring-Up & 8GB VRAM Floor Verification\n",
    "Before running Structure-from-Motion or Gaussian Splatting optimization, verify that your workstation GPU has sufficient free memory to stay within the **8GB VRAM floor** (close heavy background GPU processes such as Unity Editor or hardware-accelerated browser tabs during training)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "def verify_lab5a_environment(vram_floor_gb: float = 8.0):\n",
    "    print(\"=== CIS 536/736 Lab 5a: Environment & Hardware Audit ===\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Python Version : {sys.version.split()[0]}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"PyTorch Version: {torch.__version__}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"CUDA Available : {torch.cuda.is_available()}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "        device_id = torch.cuda.current_device()\n",
    "        device_name = torch.cuda.get_device_name(device_id)\n",
    "        free_bytes, total_bytes = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(device_id)\n",
    "        free_gb = free_bytes / (1024 ** 3)\n",
    "        total_gb = total_bytes / (1024 ** 3)\n",
    "        print(f\"GPU Device     : {device_name}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"VRAM Status    : {free_gb:.2f} GB free / {total_gb:.2f} GB total (Course Floor: {vram_floor_gb:.1f} GB)\")\n",
    "        if free_gb < 6.0:\n",
    "            print(\"WARNING: Free VRAM is below 6.0 GB. Close background GPU apps or use --data_factor 2/4 during gsplat training.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"WARNING: CUDA GPU not detected. COLMAP feature extraction will use CPU; gsplat requires a CUDA-capable GPU.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    for binary in [\"ffmpeg\", \"colmap\", \"nvidia-smi\"]:\n",
    "        path = shutil.which(binary)\n",
    "        print(f\"Binary '{binary:10s}': {'FOUND -> ' + path if path else 'NOT FOUND on PATH'}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    for pkg in [\"gsplat\", \"pxr\", \"trimesh\"]:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            __import__(pkg)\n",
    "            print(f\"Package '{pkg:9s}': INSTALLED\")\n",
    "        except ImportError:\n",
    "            print(f\"Package '{pkg:9s}': MISSING (Install via pip: gsplat / usd-core / trimesh)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "verify_lab5a_environment()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
