   "source": [
    "## Part 3: Multi-View Capture Extraction & COLMAP Structure-from-Motion (Lectures 26 & 27)\n",
    "To reconstruct a real-world object or scene in **MP 7 Part 2**, your capture dataset must satisfy three photogrammetric invariants:\n",
    "1. **Static Lighting & Locked Exposure:** Lock camera exposure/focus and avoid moving shadows.\n",
    "2. **30–50+ Multi-View Frames with 70–80% Overlap:** Orbit the subject at 2–3 elevation rings (eye-level, slightly above, slightly below) rather than panning from a stationary tripod.\n",
    "3. **Resolution Cap ($1920 \\times 1080$):** Downscale 4K video/photos to 1080p so `gsplat` optimization stays well within the **8GB VRAM floor**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cell below provides a complete, reproducible Python wrapper that:\n",
    "* Extracts 30–50 downscaled 1080p frames from a capture video via `ffmpeg`, and\n",
    "* Executes the 4-step COLMAP Structure-from-Motion pipeline (`feature_extractor`, `sequential_matcher`, `mapper`, `image_undistorter`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SFM_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"part2_colmap_sfm\"\n",
    "IMAGES_DIR = SFM_DIR / \"images\"\n",
    "SPARSE_DIR = SFM_DIR / \"sparse\"\n",
    "UNDISTORTED_DIR = SFM_DIR / \"undistorted\"\n",
    "IMAGES_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "SPARSE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract_frames_1080p(video_path: Path, output_dir: Path, target_fps: float = 2.0, max_width: int = 1920):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Extracts sharp frames from an input capture video at `target_fps` while scaling\n",
    "    width to at most 1920px (1080p) to respect the 8GB VRAM floor.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    cmd = [\n",
    "        \"ffmpeg\", \"-y\", \"-i\", str(video_path),\n",
    "        \"-vf\", f\"fps={target_fps},scale='min({max_width},iw)':-2\",\n",
    "        \"-qscale:v\", \"2\",\n",
    "        str(output_dir / \"frame_%04d.jpg\")\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    print(\"Command:\", \" \".join(cmd))\n",
    "    if video_path.exists() and shutil.which(\"ffmpeg\"):\n",
    "        subprocess.run(cmd, check=True)\n",
    "        frames = sorted(output_dir.glob(\"*.jpg\"))\n",
    "        print(f\"Extracted {len(frames)} frames to {output_dir}\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"[Dry-Run] Place your capture video at `video_path` or copy 30-50 .jpg photos into `images/`.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_colmap_pipeline_commands(scene_dir: Path, matcher: str = \"sequential\") -> list:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Constructs the canonical 4-step COLMAP Structure-from-Motion pipeline commands.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    db_path = scene_dir / \"database.db\"\n",
    "    img_dir = scene_dir / \"images\"\n",
    "    sparse_dir = scene_dir / \"sparse\"\n",
    "    undist_dir = scene_dir / \"undistorted\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    cmds = [\n",
    "        # 1. SIFT Feature Extraction with shared single-camera intrinsics\n",
    "        [\n",
    "            \"colmap\", \"feature_extractor\",\n",
    "            \"--database_path\", str(db_path),\n",
    "            \"--image_path\", str(img_dir),\n",
    "            \"--ImageReader.single_camera\", \"1\",\n",
    "            \"--ImageReader.camera_model\", \"SIMPLE_RADIAL\"\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "        # 2. Feature Matching (sequential_matcher for video frames; exhaustive_matcher for photo sets)\n",
    "        [\n",
    "            \"colmap\", f\"{matcher}_matcher\",\n",
    "            \"--database_path\", str(db_path)\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "        # 3. Sparse Bundle Adjustment (incremental triangulation & pose recovery)\n",
    "        [\n",
    "            \"colmap\", \"mapper\",\n",
    "            \"--database_path\", str(db_path),\n",
    "            \"--image_path\", str(img_dir),\n",
    "            \"--output_path\", str(sparse_dir)\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "        # 4. Undistort to ideal PINHOLE camera model for 3D Gaussian projection\n",
    "        [\n",
    "            \"colmap\", \"image_undistorter\",\n",
    "            \"--image_path\", str(img_dir),\n",
    "            \"--input_path\", str(sparse_dir / \"0\"),\n",
    "            \"--output_path\", str(undist_dir),\n",
    "            \"--output_type\", \"COLMAP\"\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    return cmds\n",
    "\n",
    "for step_idx, cmd in enumerate(build_colmap_pipeline_commands(SFM_DIR), start=1):\n",
    "    print(f\"Step {step_idx}: {' '.join(cmd)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 4: The 3D Gaussian Splat Primitive, Adaptive Density Control & Local `gsplat` Training\n",
    "In **Lecture 26**, we studied how 3D Gaussian Splatting avoids the millions of per-ray MLP queries of NeRFs by representing the scene explicitly as $N$ anisotropic 3D Gaussians:\n",
    "1. **3D Position (Mean):** $\\mu_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^3$\n",
    "2. **Positive Semi-Definite 3D Covariance:** Factored into a diagonal scaling matrix $S_i = \\text{diag}(s_x, s_y, s_z)$ and a rotation matrix $R_i(q_i)$ derived from a unit quaternion $q_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^4$:\n",
    "   $$\\Sigma_i = R_i S_i S_i^\\top R_i^\\top$$\n",
    "3. **Opacity & Volumetric Alpha Blending:** $\\alpha_i = \\sigma(\\tilde{\\alpha}_i) \\in (0, 1)$, composited front-to-back in $16 \\times 16$ screen tiles with early ray termination when accumulated transmittance $T_i = \\prod_{j=1}^{i-1}(1 - \\alpha_j)$ drops near zero:\n",
    "   $$C = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i \\alpha_i \\prod_{j=1}^{i-1} (1 - \\alpha_j)$$\n",
    "4. **Adaptive Density Control:** During optimization against $\\mathcal{L} = (1 - \\lambda)\\mathcal{L}_1 + \\lambda \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{D-SSIM}}$, Gaussians with view-space positional gradient $\\|\\nabla_{\\mu_{2D}} \\mathcal{L}\\|_2 > \\tau_{\\text{pos}}$ are **cloned** (if $\\max(S_i) \\le \\tau_S$) or **split** (if $\\max(S_i) > \\tau_S$), while transparent splats ($\\alpha_i < \\epsilon_\\alpha$) are **pruned**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cell below to verify the differentiable PyTorch math for covariance construction, front-to-back alpha blending, adaptive density masks, and `.ply` export."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def quat_to_rotmat(quats: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Converts normalized quaternions (w, x, y, z) of shape (N, 4) to 3x3 rotation matrices (N,
